      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic ocr and layout extraction task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nThe initial file extract_text.py is already implemented. Read it before generating the remaining files, and leave it unchanged.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] extract_text.py - extracts plain text from a scanned document image\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] extract_layout.py - extracts blocks, lines, tables, or layout elements from a document\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] extract_tables.py - extracts table cells and row structure from a document\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] extract_key_values.py - extracts key-value pairs from a form-like document\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] document_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for OCR and Layout Extraction\n6. [HELPER] document_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for OCR and Layout Extraction\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] ocr_translate.py - Translate extracted OCR text\n8. [LATER-STEP] ocr_safety.py - Check extracted document text for unsafe content\n9. [LATER-STEP] document_field_extraction.py - Extract structured fields from OCR-normalized document text\n10. [LATER-STEP] ocr_embedding.py - Embed extracted document sections for semantic retrieval\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
